{
  "note": "Frames left out of the media picked by build-catalog.mjs, so the flip-book animation (and the thumbnail, frame 1 of what is left) stays in one consistent line style and framing. Key: \"<source>/<sourceId>\"; value: {\"<upstream frame number>\": \"<reason>\"}. An exercise left with one frame is shown static; a candidate left with none falls back to the next candidate. How the list was made: README.md, \"Frame consistency\".",
  "reasons": {
    "bold-outline": "Redrawn frame with heavy, often hollow strokes (opaque edges around a semi-transparent core) and none of the anti-aliased edge the first frame has; usually also re-framed at another scale. Triage: under 3% of the stroke pixels at alpha 17-63.",
    "thin-strokes": "Thinner, doubled or partly translucent strokes that read faint or grey next to the first frame. Triage: the stroke alpha histogram is off the curve all first frames sit on.",
    "composite": "Two poses drawn side by side in one frame: does not animate with the other frames.",
    "framing": "Same style but a different view, scale or position: the animation jumps."
  },
